          "body": "{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"status_code\": 200,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"file_name\": \"Employee-Handbook.pdf\",\n    \"summary_type\": \"detailed\",\n    \"summary\": \"The document is an employee handbook that outlines the company's policies and procedures. It begins with a welcome and introduction to the company's mission and culture. It covers employment basics, including contract types (full-time, part-time, temporary, indefinite) and equal opportunity employment, emphasizing non-discrimination and accommodations. The recruitment and selection process is detailed, along with background checks and employee referral programs with associated bonuses. Attendance expectations and workplace policies are described, including confidentiality and data protection, harassment and violence prevention, workplace safety and health, smoking and drug-free workplace rules. The Employee Code of Conduct addresses dress code, cyber security, internet and cell phone usage, corporate email, social media use, conflict of interest, employee relationships, fraternization, employment of relatives, workplace visitors, and solicitation and distribution. Compensation and development sections explain compensation status (exempt vs non-exempt), overtime, payroll, performance management, managerial expectations, training and development budgets, benefits and perks, employee health, workers' compensation, work-from-home and remote working arrangements, employee expense reimbursement, company car and parking policies, and company-issued equipment. Time-related provisions detail working hours, paid time off (PTO), holidays, sick leave, long-term illness under FMLA, bereavement leave, jury duty and voting leave, and parental leave (maternity and paternity). The handbook also describes procedures for leaving the company, including progressive discipline, resignation, tuition or relocation reimbursement, forced resignation, termination, and providing references. Finally, it notes annual policy revisions and requires employee acknowledgment of receipt and understanding.\",\n    \"main_topic\": \"Employee Handbook and Company Policies\",\n    \"keywords\": [\n      \"Employee Handbook\",\n      \"Workplace Policies\",\n      \"Compensation\",\n      \"Benefits\",\n      \"Leave\",\n      \"Code of Conduct\"\n    ]\n  }\n}"
        }
      ]
